From: Local rebuild <local@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 23:15:00 +0200
Subject: Bound and timestamp the live appsrc queue

The relay pushes every input sample into appsrc while disabling appsrc's
need-data and enough-data signals. With the default unlimited buffer count,
non-blocking pushes and non-leaky queue, stale live-video frames accumulate
whenever the output falls behind.

Use time-format segments and timestamp missing buffer timestamps. Limit the
queue to two buffers and discard its oldest buffer when full so latency stays
bounded. Disable the byte and time thresholds so the buffer-count limit is
the single queue policy.
---
 src/v4l2-relayd.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/v4l2-relayd.c b/src/v4l2-relayd.c
index 8ff5ce9..6c5850b 100644
--- a/src/v4l2-relayd.c
+++ b/src/v4l2-relayd.c
@@ -476,9 +476,14 @@ output_pipeline_create ()
   appsrc = gst_bin_get_by_name (GST_BIN (pipeline), "appsrc");
   g_object_set (appsrc,
                 "stream-type", GST_APP_STREAM_TYPE_STREAM,
-                "format", GST_FORMAT_DEFAULT,
+                "format", GST_FORMAT_TIME,
                 "is-live", TRUE,
+                "do-timestamp", TRUE,
+                "max-buffers", G_GUINT64_CONSTANT (2),
+                "max-bytes", G_GUINT64_CONSTANT (0),
+                "max-time", G_GUINT64_CONSTANT (0),
+                "leaky-type", GST_APP_LEAKY_TYPE_DOWNSTREAM,
                 "emit-signals", FALSE,
                 NULL);
   gst_object_unref (appsrc);

